<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis shows further strength.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis shows further strength.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A lack of farmer sales and continued mill demand led to further firmness in basis bids across Kansas and Oklahoma, grain merchandisers said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;There's a lot of mills right now that really need some grain and they just can't get any. I'd say premiums are going to stay firm until the new crop comes on line,&quot; a north-central Oklahoma dealer said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, one south-central Kansas dealer said local meteorologists were forecasting rain later Thursday in dry areas of western Kansas.  </p>
